{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:033P:prose-0002", "parent_tag": "033P", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe phrase ``regular in codimension <MATH_0001>'' makes sense since we have seen\nin Section <REF_0001> that if <MATH_0002> is irreducible\nclosed with generic point <MATH_0003>, then\n<MATH_0004>. For example condition\n<MATH_0005> means that for every generic point <MATH_0006> of an irreducible\ncomponent of <MATH_0007> the local ring <MATH_0008> is a field.\nBut for general Noetherian schemes it can happen that the regular locus\nof <MATH_0009> is badly behaved, so care has to be taken.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$k$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-catenary}", "MATH_0002": "$Y \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$x$", "MATH_0004": "$\\dim(\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}) = \\text{codim}(Y, X)$", "MATH_0005": "$(R_0)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\eta \\in X$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, \\eta}$", "MATH_0009": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:f2ba0c64ba8964801aa87a24d4831cd9a3b4a02890e56be8c01ffbda379d8e91", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:44f333783fe05e51073e6b8680cc959fbbd74aca407053b629e061bb331421ab", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1dc69f1bafd23746dadd91faa8a09c615b616ada90288dec3f70ca90881e68ac"}
